{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny","id":1478852,"title":"How many of you think that Augustus Giovanni was diaberlized by one of his progeny?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-14T09:46:11-07:00","id":1478852,"title":"How many of you think that Augustus Giovanni was diaberlized by one of his progeny?","content":"My two bits is that is what happened to Augustus and it would be a fitting end to him and it was maybe Ambrigino Giovanni who did the deed to complete his necromantic research? or maybe I'm completely way off base and he is just hiding from his clan out of fear that his plans went seriously awry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-14-2022, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T09:54:17-07:00","id":1478854,"title":"","content":"I think that August was diablerized at the Family Dinner (reunion). I am not sure by who, I would think Ambrogino was killed with the other elder Giovanni in the uprising of the ancilla and neonates. Maybe there was some oblivion ceremony where his soul was shared among the clan somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;[Mankind] lives in a survived yet always uncertainly surviving world. All that is has survived where it might not have survived. Every world is and will always be a Noah's ark.&quot; -John Fowles, <i>The Aristos</i>","edited":{"userid":2405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2405-astriarch","user":"Astriarch","date":". 04-14-2022, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2405-astriarch","name":"Astriarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2405_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T11:44:14-07:00","id":1478856,"title":"","content":"It would be ironic, and honestly that alone makes me think that's what happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T12:45:26-07:00","id":1478860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astriarch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478854#post1478854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that August was diablerized at the Family Dinner (reunion). I am not sure by who, I would think Ambrogino was killed with the other elder Giovanni in the uprising of the ancilla and neonates. Maybe there was some oblivion ceremony where his soul was shared among the clan somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ambrogino is alive, he is mentioned a couple times in Cults, one time as an advisor to the Capuchin.<br /> <br /> Speaking about the Capuchin, I do like the idea of him devouring Augustus' soul. The Capuchin being Lazarus or some other ancient vampire (though certainly not Japhet or Byzar, they suck, especially the latter). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T12:51:34-07:00","id":1478862,"title":"","content":"I think it would be fitting if it was one of the Cappadocian or Harbinger of skull elders who ate augustus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27369,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","user":"The smiling gun-knight","date":". 04-22-2022, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T12:54:56-07:00","id":1478864,"title":"","content":"I thought the Capuchin was just a false identity shared by Lazarus, Japheth and Byzar. Or did they retcon that for V5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T13:05:23-07:00","id":1478865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478864#post1478864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Capuchin was just a false identity shared by Lazarus, Japheth and Byzar. Or did they retcon that for V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not specified in anyway. His identity is purposefully left very unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T13:25:01-07:00","id":1478868,"title":"","content":"We do know that Lazarus and Ambridgino did have a relationship and helped each other in there research and it makes me wonder if he aided other Giovanni discretely and Augustus turned a blind eye to it.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-14-2022, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T14:06:47-07:00","id":1478871,"title":"","content":"I assume that some Harbingers would be peevish if it didn't happen their way. It would be the climax of their vendetta, unless that's still to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T15:30:40-07:00","id":1478873,"title":"","content":"Personally I subscribe to the idea that Augustus was sacrificed in a ritual that bound the Bloodlines together into a single Clan, hence why the various Bloodlines lost their old Weaknesses for the Giovanni Weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T05:56:06-07:00","id":1478901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478864#post1478864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Capuchin was just a false identity shared by Lazarus, Japheth and Byzar. Or did they retcon that for V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>To the best of my knowledge, that idea was first offered in V20's &quot;The Black Hand: A Guide To The Tal'mahe'ra,&quot; which was a deliberately metaplot-agnostic &quot;take what works and leave the rest&quot; sort of book.<br /> <br /> You're left with wiggle room to make the character what you need him to be, by design.<br /> <br /> As familiar as all the descendants of Clan Cappadocian are with incomplete diableries and their long term vengenace-flavored consequences, I can't see anyone putting teeth into Augie. Why run the risk of him having learned how to cheat death the same way, when he's had nearly six hundred years to think about it? With the talent this clan can assemble, he's much easier to control if his soul is bound in something at the moment of Final Death rather than possibly allowed to run free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T06:08:45-07:00","id":1478903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478873#post1478873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I subscribe to the idea that Augustus was sacrificed in a ritual that bound the Bloodlines together into a single Clan, hence why the various Bloodlines lost their old Weaknesses for the Giovanni Weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea best. I don\u2019t think they need or want another 3rd-generation patriarch, and it\u2019s fitting for them to be perhaps the only clan whose head is unambiguously and incontrovertibly dead. Also, what better way to bind these disparate branches of the family together than to share his power equally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T07:22:38-07:00","id":1478905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478873#post1478873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I subscribe to the idea that Augustus was sacrificed in a ritual that bound the Bloodlines together into a single Clan, hence why the various Bloodlines lost their old Weaknesses for the Giovanni Weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can also helps to explain why the Hecata don't experience the Beckoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T12:13:52-07:00","id":1478917,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle Augustus was killed by the PCs during Gehenna. They used the specter of Cappadocius in conjunction with Augustus\u2019 true blood and another primordial artifact while fighting his enslaved wraiths in the underworld. When the ritual was completed Augustus\u2019 power was momentarily broken and 50 million ghosts jumped on him tearing him to pieces and dragging his rotten soul to the labyrinth. <br /> For a new V5 game I slightly retconned this with Ambrogino betraying Augustus, weakening his wards and allowing the other factions of the clan of death to attack him. In the end Augustus was swallowed by the spectre horde and no one knows what happened to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T12:16:26-07:00","id":1478918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478903#post1478903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this idea best. I don\u2019t think they need or want another 3rd-generation patriarch, and it\u2019s fitting for them to be perhaps the only clan whose head is unambiguously and incontrovertibly dead. Also, what better way to bind these disparate branches of the family together than to share his power equally.</div> </div> </div> </div> The only clan whose 3rd gen progenitor is sure to be dead is Ravnos. What really happened to Augustus (and to Cappadocius for that matter) is not clear. As of the current metaplot Augustus may be dead, captured or even at large, plotting his revenge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T13:31:03-07:00","id":1478920,"title":"","content":"'The only clan whose 3rd gen progenitor is sure to be dead is Ravnos' can we be sure that was ravnos and not an illusion the antediluvian made.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T14:01:31-07:00","id":1478921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478920#post1478920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'The only clan whose 3rd gen progenitor is sure to be dead is Ravnos' can we be sure that was ravnos and not an illusion the antediluvian made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Official canon has declared Zapathasura destroyed, but they acknowledge this as an option Storytellers are welcome to go with instead. I think the in-game logic is that the Ravnos Antediluvian was in a Frenzy during his rampage, and thus was unable to pull off such a deception with Chimerstry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-15T19:34:38-07:00","id":1478931,"title":"","content":"Yeah [Ravnos'] death is pretty certain by default, especially in V5 given the Ravnos' new Clan Flaw.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T09:08:17-07:00","id":1478957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478905#post1478905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That can also helps to explain why the Hecata don't experience the Beckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T06:14:42-07:00","id":1479011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1478921#post1478921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I think the in-game logic is that the Ravnos Antediluvian was in a Frenzy during his rampage, and thus was unable to pull off such a deception with Chimerstry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wich is pretty stupid, considering Zappy not only had Chimestry, but Animalism, and several of its power basically makes you either immune to Frenzy or allows you too keep your sanity, ride the Wave, or simply toss out your beast (I actually had a funny session where tho' Zappy escaped destruction, his P'o/Beast - was a bitly crossowery story with KotE - wandered away, and the party in service of the antediluvian (and other ancients) had to track it down and capture the host tiger, that became a Raksahsa-like demon) out to pester others<br /> Another flaw in that theory, the Week of Nightmares was around most likely Monday, June 28 to Sunday, July 4, 1999. Thats... darn long time for a frenzy! And against the three of the eldest Kuei-jin Bodhisattvas Zappy used a plathora of powers not just brute might, fang and claws...<br /> Thats not really possible if you are out of your mind in a Frenzy<br /> <br /> And... there is that little V5 thing, called &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Funny to think, Zapathasura became Venom-like<br /> Anyhow, Malkav survived destruction after he was torn to shreds, and several of his children gathered and consumed his blood, shileding it from the sun, in themselves... Maybe Zappy pulled a Malkav<br /> All and all, it will be forever hard to swallow for almost everyone he&quot;died&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-17-2022, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T07:08:53-07:00","id":1479012,"title":"","content":"The books say he's dead, but I imagine there's a lot of beings in the WoD who assume that it's a ruse or that if any vampire could have pulled off the the trick of faking a death, it would be the vampire who has completely mastered chimerstry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T08:30:39-07:00","id":1479013,"title":"","content":"A headcanon of mine is that no Antediluvian is permanently dead if their bloodlines still exist. They just end up in a non-physical torpor like state. With enough time and if enough potent Blood, Sorcery, Unobtanium or Plot Devices are gathered together, Ravnos will be able to awaken and take physical form again. Or maybe he will just choose to continue existing in the Blood, though with greater conscience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T10:19:34-07:00","id":1479019,"title":"","content":"The antidevulians certainly make final death just a minor inconvenience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T11:53:47-07:00","id":1479023,"title":"","content":"Which brings up an old question: is Ventrue really dead? Supposedly he died way back during the 2nd city, which is very hard to believe. With no Antedeluvian to periodically pop out baby 4rth gens, the Ventrue should have long since gone extinct, or, at a minimum, faded into a tiny, thin-blooded bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T12:13:34-07:00","id":1479025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1479023#post1479023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which brings up an old question: is Ventrue really dead? Supposedly he died way back during the 2nd city, which is very hard to believe. With no Antedeluvian to periodically pop out baby 4rth gens, the Ventrue should have long since gone extinct, or, at a minimum, faded into a tiny, thin-blooded bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div> it certainly makes things complicated in regards to certain Antedeluvian fates. I think that Ventrue nevered suffered final death and like Brujah resides in a new form and periodically makes it\u2019s presence felt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T08:57:44-07:00","id":1479087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1479011#post1479011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wich is pretty stupid, considering Zappy not only had Chimestry, but Animalism, and several of its power basically makes you either immune to Frenzy or allows you too keep your sanity, ride the Wave, or simply toss out your beast (I actually had a funny session where tho' Zappy escaped destruction, his P'o/Beast - was a bitly crossowery story with KotE - wandered away, and the party in service of the antediluvian (and other ancients) had to track it down and capture the host tiger, that became a Raksahsa-like demon) out to pester others<br /> Another flaw in that theory, the Week of Nightmares was around most likely Monday, June 28 to Sunday, July 4, 1999. Thats... darn long time for a frenzy! And against the three of the eldest Kuei-jin Bodhisattvas Zappy used a plathora of powers not just brute might, fang and claws...<br /> Thats not really possible if you are out of your mind in a Frenzy<br /> <br /> And... there is that little V5 thing, called &quot;Blood of Zapathasura&quot; - Thick, <b>sentient</b> ropes of his vitae stained the ground in Bangladesh where he fell. The noonday sun <b>did not destroy it all</b>. You own a small vial containing the Blood of the Ravnos Antediluvian. What you do with this vitae is up to you, and what it does to anyone who imbibes it is up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Funny to think, Zapathasura became Venom-like<br /> Anyhow, Malkav survived destruction after he was torn to shreds, and several of his children gathered and consumed his blood, shileding it from the sun, in themselves... Maybe Zappy pulled a Malkav<br /> All and all, it will be forever hard to swallow for almost everyone he&quot;died&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for the delay in response, been busy the last few days.<br /> <br /> Beyond being the kind of person who prefers to stick with canon when it has been established, I'm not especially attached to the idea that Zapathasura was definitely destroyed. But I do have some thoughts regarding your response:<br /> <br /> There are Animalism powers that help you resist or make you immune to Frenzy, but the only one that he would be guaranteed to have would be the level 5 power that lets you put your Beast into someone else; if there was no viable target when he awoke, he might have been overcome by Frenzy before being able to avoid it. If Zapathasura had focused on other Elder-level Animalism powers rather than the ones that help control Frenzy, he may have just been out of luck.<br /> <br /> I do agree that it's a long time for a Frenzy, and I haven't read the source material in a while, but it's possible that he may have become a wight instead of just being in a Frenzy. Or it might have been a supernaturally-provoked Frenzy that lasted longer as a result (and thus adds a layer of mystery and scheming to the whole event: who could possibly manipulate an Antediluvian like that?).<br /> <br /> Again, it's been a while since I read the full account of the Week of Nightmares, but depending on what kinds of powers he mustered against the three Bodhisattvas, they may have been ones that he could use in a Frenzy. Stuff like Blood Magic is generally off the table when you're a wight or in a Frenzy, but any power that you can use instinctively is available. Thus, even if the supernatural powers Zapathasura was using against the Wan Kuei were extremely powerful, he wouldn't need to be in control of himself if they were simply instances of supernatural &quot;brute force&quot; being tossed around.<br /> <br /> All of this sets aside a couple of other possible factors. Firstly, fighting against the Bodhisattvas may have used up enough of the supernatural power that Zapathasura had at his disposal that he didn't have the strength left to alter reality itself in such a fashion. Or it might be that the &quot;spirit-nukes&quot; used by the Technocracy disrupted his powers in some way that he *couldn't* use his Chimerstry to alter reality in order to escape the situation. That sort of thing seems like a matter of Storyteller fiat than anything else, but I'm inclined to think that if there's anything that could overpower an Antediluvian and take it down, the entire might of the Technocracy being aimed at it would be one of the possibilities.<br /> <br /> The Blood of Zapathasura is one thing that throws a wrench in a lot of what I've just said, and I really feel that it's a weird choice on V5's part to have something like that exist. Having someone collect vials of the Antediluvian's fallen vitae and then getting out of dodge before the whole situation went nuclear is a bit of a stretch but not unbelievable. But having the Antediluvian's vitae continuing to exist and even surviving direct sunlight is an extremely odd choice IMO, and does seem to directly defy the established canon around Zapathasura's demise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which does kind of lead into the wider point I wanted to discuss, which is that I personally don't like the Antediluvian's being treated as transcendental beings by default, as literal gods that are something fundamentally different from their childer. I like the Antediluvians to simply be bigger, badder vampires by default; far more powerful due to their age and Generation, but not operating by special rules without specific circumstances explaining how they have become something different/more. And thus, while some Antediluvians might have found a way to change into something other than a vampire, or live in through their descendants in some special way, I like to imagine that many of the Antediluvians are still &quot;only&quot; vampires, even if they represent the pinnacle of the power a vampire can achieve. In particular, the ones that focus more on temporal power or human experiences than spiritual development.<br /> <br /> So we have Antediluvians like Tzimisce, Lasombra, and Cappadocius that are explicitly described as becoming something else, or attempting to do so at least. Then we have others where such an evolution is strongly implied, like with Malkav and Saulot. But when it comes to Antediluvians like Arikel or Absimiliard, I imagine that they have never really been focused on that kind of transcendence, and thus have remained fundamentally like other vampires, just more powerful. And that's kind of the fate I imagine for the Ventrue Antediluvian if they survived and faked their destruction; either living in the Antediluvian equivalent of retirement, or quietly manipulating events from the shadows.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T10:23:57-07:00","id":1479136,"title":"","content":"My homebrew:<br /> <br /> The family gathered at Familly Reunion and held a ritual feast on the body and soul of Augustus.<br /> He wasn't diabolized by one vampire.<br /> His blood and soul served a greater purpose. Everyone participating in the feast became one family. Hecata. And their descendants also underwent a transformation, for so great is the power of the antediluvian blood.<br /> <br /> Thanks to this, we have a new Hecata bloodline, and there are some vampires from the original bloodlines whose ancestors did not take part in the ritual feast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25881-mr-stick","name":"Mr. Stick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T11:36:26-07:00","id":1479139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Stick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1479136#post1479136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My homebrew:<br /> <br /> The family gathered at Familly Reunion and held a ritual feast on the body and soul of Augustus.<br /> He wasn't diabolized by one vampire.<br /> His blood and soul served a greater purpose. Everyone participating in the feast became one family. Hecata. And their descendants also underwent a transformation, for so great is the power of the antediluvian blood.<br /> <br /> Thanks to this, we have a new Hecata bloodline, and there are some vampires from the original bloodlines whose ancestors did not take part in the ritual feast.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting take on what happened to Augustus Giovanni and how the disparte lineages are now changing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T23:28:26-07:00","id":1479163,"title":"","content":"I'd rather it not known. <br /> Maybe my players can chomp him, or influence who chomped him, or discover who chomped him and correspondingly chomp them. Actually writing an answer denies me a lot of fun, I'd rather have a WhoDunnit list of likely suspects. <br /> <br /> Ravana also should be as ambiguous as possible. If anything, the best scenario for that is -didn't happen- because, while metaplot is cool at times, it does shit on a lot of stuff. <br /> <br /> Antes and ancient methuselahs work best when they're unknown. History works best for storytellers when it's as unreliable as it can get away with. That way STs have maximum leway to posit their TRUE canon to players who don't already know it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T15:47:08-07:00","id":1479448,"title":"","content":"So you find giving ancients getting stated limiting also My Wife Is Scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T12:24:55-07:00","id":1479498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1479448#post1479448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you find giving ancients getting stated limiting also My Wife Is Scary.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I don't want to see an Antes character sheet because they're just too important, but I'm not entirely opposed to a 4th or 5th gen's sheet so long as it'd done well. Personally, I don't like canon characters, and I think the less influence they have on a large scale the better. But I won't begrudge a well written and self-contained city book or prefabricated chronicle for those who like to use them directly or for inspiration. I think city books should ideally be possibilities and inspiration rather than canonical too, because I don't think anyone's game should be more valid than anyone else's just because they got picked as author, but that's another topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T17:52:06-07:00","id":1479519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1478852-how-many-of-you-think-that-augustus-giovanni-was-diaberlized-by-one-of-his-progeny?p=1479498#post1479498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I don't want to see an Antes character sheet because they're just too important, but I'm not entirely opposed to a 4th or 5th gen's sheet so long as it'd done well. Personally, I don't like canon characters, and I think the less influence they have on a large scale the better. But I won't begrudge a well written and self-contained city book or prefabricated chronicle for those who like to use them directly or for inspiration. I think city books should ideally be possibilities and inspiration rather than canonical too, because I don't think anyone's game should be more valid than anyone else's just because they got picked as author, but that's another topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an old saying that if it has stats, it can be killed. You don't make a sheet for something that's supposed to be too powerful to be challenged unless your very point is that it can be challenged. And killed.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean that stating out the Antes is necessarily limiting or something, but that it changes the assumptions on how they'll work in a game. Which can be good or bad, but is a change nonetheless.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I would like to see options on stats for them, things that cover different takes and themes on how to incorporate the Antes in a game as characters that can significantly interact with and challenge the PCs in some way, but at least three ideas for each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-26T09:06:37-07:00","id":1479549,"title":"","content":"I think at best that 5th or 6th generation clan members should be stated at and maybe there much younger then there older generational peers. They should be the heralds of what a truly powerful ancient vampire can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name